      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVES",
          "content": "To illustrate the utility of crowdsourcing for occupational health surveillance."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Amazon Mechanical Turk was used to recruit and obtain information from employed persons with asthma, who answered questions about work-asthma interactions."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Data collection from 60 subjects required only a few hours. Participants spent on average 7 minutes responding to seven questions (one optional) and used an average of 708 words. Work exacerbation, interference of asthma with work, and suggested workplace accommodation are frequent (83% reported at least one interaction)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "The full spectrum of work-asthma interactions should be considered. Modern crowdsourcing methods have considerable potential as occupational health surveillance tools because of their effectiveness; efficiency and financial viability are additional important advantages."
        }
      ]},
